      "summary": "The tests map to the listed criteria and cover the main calculation, blocking, discrepancy, session authorization, and simulated decision paths. However, approval accepts a self-consistent fabricated draft, and a test currently codifies that behavior despite the malformed-input and provenance requirements.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Finance/ReserveCalculator.cs",
          "line": 180,
          "message": "AC4: Reject hand-built drafts without validated report provenance; arithmetic consistency alone allows malformed drafts to be approved.",
          "confidence": 0.86,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "Review accepts a public ReserveDraft and IsConsistentCalculation checks only its supplied fields and arithmetic; it does not verify that Calculate produced the draft from the source reports.",
            "failureScenario": "A caller constructs a ReadyForReview draft with fabricated report IDs and internally consistent lines and total, then a finance reviewer approves it. Review records the approval even though the draft was never calculated from utilization or rate reports. The test Approve_refuses_hand_built_or_tampered_draft explicitly expects this fabricated draft to be approved."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
